  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment should establish a strong multimodal baseline using the highest-capacity choices across all design dimensions: scgpt (pretrained single-cell foundation model) for RNA, imagenet_vit_l (largest image encoder) for images, transformer aggregation (most expressive for multiprofile), and weighted fusion (most flexible modality combining). This tests whether the full multimodal pipeline can achieve strong validation accuracy and provides a ceiling reference. If it performs well, subsequent experiments can ablate individual components (encoder, aggregation, fusion) to identify what drives performance. If it underperforms, it signals that complexity is a bottleneck and simpler alternatives (e.g., resnet50, avgpool, concat) should be explored. This is the most informative single experiment under a 10-run budget because it simultaneously validates the multimodal hypothesis and anchors the search space."
}

